# No empty constructors

**Never add an empty constructor** — not `public`, not `protected`, and especially not `private ClassName() { }`.

Do not add them to block instantiation, for “utility class” style, to satisfy IDE templates, or out of habit. They add noise and are not required in this codebase.

## Omit the constructor

If the class has no other constructors, **declare none**. Java supplies a default no-arg constructor when one is actually needed.

```java
// ❌ BAD — never add this pattern
public final class QuestDialogCheckpoints {
    private QuestDialogCheckpoints() {
    }

    public static List<QuestDialogCheckpoint> load(...) { ... }
}

// ✅ GOOD — static helpers only, no constructor at all
public final class QuestDialogCheckpoints {
    public static List<QuestDialogCheckpoint> load(...) { ... }
}
```

Same for instance classes with no special construction needs:

```java
// ❌ BAD
public class QuestStepEngine {
    public QuestStepEngine() {
    }
}

// ✅ GOOD
public class QuestStepEngine {
}
```

## Only exception: a framework or deserializer **requires** it

Add an empty constructor **only** when you have confirmed the API will not work without it:

| Case | Visibility | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Bukkit `JavaPlugin` subclass | `public` | Required by the plugin loader |
| Deserializer needs no-arg **and** other constructors exist | `public` or `protected` | SnakeYAML bean with a typed constructor for scalars |

If you are unsure, **do not add** a constructor — check how the type is loaded first.

## Do not use private ctors on static-only types

```java
// ❌ BAD — private empty ctor “utility class” pattern
public final class QuestLoreDisplay {
    private QuestLoreDisplay() { }

    public static void addQuestLore(...) { ... }
}

// ✅ GOOD — no constructor; put helpers on the natural owner when possible
public final class QuestLoreDisplay {
    public static void addQuestLore(...) { ... }
}
```

Prefer moving static helpers to an existing manager, command, or window instead of a new `*Helper` / `*Display` type (see `prefer-few-service-classes.mdc`).

## Agent checklist

Before finishing a Java edit, search your diff for `() {\s*}` or `() {}` on constructors. **Delete** any empty constructor you added unless the exception above applies. **Do not** re-add `private Foo() {}` when touching utility classes.
